<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viceroy of India</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as viceroy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A viceroy is an official who governs a country or province in the name of a monarch. The title is best known for the Viceroy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the head of British government in India after 1858, who governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-civil-service">Indian Civil Service</a>. Similar offices existed in the Spanish viceroyalties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and in Portuguese India, and the term is also used for provincial governors in other empires, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-kush">Viceroy of Kush</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india.jpg" alt="Viceroy of India" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greentubing · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Governor-General_of_India_(1885%E2%80%931947).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1861 the Canning Award, issued by Lord Canning as <b>Viceroy of India</b>, confirmed the separation of the two states, with Zanzibar to pay Oman an annual subsidy of 40,000 Maria Theresa thalers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Sultanate of Zanzibar · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Canning Award of 1861, arbitrated by the <b>Viceroy of India</b>, confirmed the split, with Zanzibar paying Muscat an annual subsidy.</blockquote><a href="/state/sultanate-of-muscat-and-oman">Sultanate of Muscat and Oman</a></li></ul></section>
